# Godot GDScript addon (reflaxe.GDScript, 1.0.0-beta)
#
# Compiles the whole library to GDScript 2.0. Each `dropecho.noise.*` class
# becomes a global `class_name` script — the GDScript analog of the JS build's
# global `@:expose` — so Godot code can call e.g. `Perlin.new(...).value(x, y)`.
#
# `-D generate_godot_plugin` makes the compiler also emit `plugin.cfg` and the
# `@tool` EditorPlugin (`plugin.gd`) into the output dir, so it installs and
# enables as a normal addon under Project Settings > Plugins. The library is
# pure math (no Godot types), so no Godot bindings generator is needed.

-lib gdscript

-D generate_godot_plugin
-D godot_plugin_name=dropecho.noise
-D godot_plugin_description=A library of 2D noise generation tools.
-D godot_plugin_author=vantreeseba
-D godot_plugin_version=0.5.2

-D gdscript-output=dist/godot/addons/dropecho_noise
